The LM358’s slew‑rate limits the sinusoidal output at 20 kHz.  
Using the typical slew‑rate SR ≈ 0.5 V/µs:

$$V_{pp,\max} \approx \frac{SR}{\pi f}
               = \frac{0.5\times10^{6}\;\text{V/s}}{\pi \times 20\times10^{3}\;\text{Hz}}
               \approx 8\;\text{V}_{pp}$$

So, on a 15 V supply the LM358 can deliver roughly **8 V peak‑to‑peak** (≈ 4 V peak) at 20 kHz under typical conditions. (With the minimum guaranteed SR of 0.3 V/µs the swing would be ≈ 4.8 Vpp.)
